      "text": "The bug is that the legacy Aqua `commutator` function doesn't accept `DensityMatrix` objects. The commutator of two matrices is `AB - BA`, so I compute it directly from the `.data` arrays.\n\n```python\nfrom qiskit import QuantumCircuit\nfrom qiskit.quantum_info import DensityMatrix\nfrom qiskit.aqua.operators.legacy import commutator\n\ncirc0 = QuantumCircuit(1)\ncirc1 = QuantumCircuit(1)\n\ncirc0.x(0)\ndm0 = DensityMatrix.from_instruction(circ0)\n\ncirc1.z(0)\ndm1 = DensityMatrix.from_instruction(circ1)\n\n# FIX: commutator() from qiskit.aqua legacy does not accept DensityMatrix objects -> compute the matrix commutator AB - BA directly from the .data arrays, because the commutator of two matrices is defined as dm0*dm1 - dm1*dm0\ncomm = dm0.data @ dm1.data - dm1.data @ dm0.data\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
